    "ruling": {
     "cause": "implementation",
     "answer": "Revise the plan and the fix. The line-113 change is necessary, but it does not fix the test under `npm test`. That script, already in HEAD 4e96047's package.json, sets PI_DURABLE_CLAUDE=/bin/false and PI_DURABLE_CODEX=/bin/false. `binaryFor` (cards.mjs:96-100) reads those from process.env and ignores the env passed to `installed()`, so the fake PATH is never used. /bin/false does not exist on macOS (only /usr/bin/false does), so claude counts as not installed, gets skipped, and no block is written (1 !== 2). Keep the line-113 change and also neutralise the override inside this test. Save PI_DURABLE_CLAUDE, PI_DURABLE_CODEX and PI_DURABLE_PI, delete them from process.env before the two provisionHost calls, and restore them in a finally block. That is a test-only change. The alternative is to have `installed()` resolve the binary from its `env` argument, but that changes cards.mjs and needs the plan to allow it. Then change the gate so it runs with the npm test environment (`PI_DURABLE_ALERT=none PI_DURABLE_CLAUDE=/bin/false PI_DURABLE_CODEX=/bin/false node --test test/provision.test.mjs`), not with the variables unset.",
     "evidence": "package.json:50 test script: `PI_DURABLE_ALERT=none PI_DURABLE_CLAUDE=/bin/false PI_DURABLE_CODEX=/bin/false node --test test/*.test.mjs`. HEAD's script already had both /bin/false overrides; the working tree only adds PI_DURABLE_ALERT. `ls /bin/false` gives No such file or directory; /usr/bin/false exists. Running test/provision.test.mjs alone with the line-113 change and those variables set gives `not ok 6 - provision --host`, # fail 1. With the variables unset it gives 6/6. cards.mjs:96-109: binaryFor reads process.env.PI_DURABLE_*, and installed() does `if (command.includes('/')) return runnable(command)`, which never looks at the fake PATH. The plan named this leak itself and wrongly ruled that it 'does not cause this failure', and the test plan's gate ran with the variables unset, so it missed the case npm test runs.",
     "by": "Arbiter"
    },
